<section class="shell band faq">
  <h2>Questions about the book</h2>

  <details>
    <summary>Where can I buy Effort-less Self-Care?</summary>
    <div class="answer-body">
      <p>Through <a href="https://www.barnesandnoble.com/w/effortless-self-care-reem-glasco/1149690519">Barnes
      &amp; Noble</a>. It is written by Reem Glasco, LPC-S, a Licensed Professional Counselor
      Supervisor in Texas.</p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <details>
    <summary>What is the difference between the book and the Reset journal?</summary>
    <div class="answer-body">
      <p><em>Effort-less Self-Care: 7 Easy Steps to Calm and Connection</em> sets out the
      practice. <em>Reset: 7 Effortless Self-Care Practices to Cultivate Calm and Connection</em>
      is the self-paced journal that carries the same seven practices with prompts and space to
      write, aimed particularly at therapists and healers.</p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <details>
    <summary>How long does the practice take?</summary>
    <div class="answer-body">
      <p>A few minutes. Two of the steps have a built-in pause, thirty seconds with a hand on
      your chest and seventeen seconds of sensory grounding, and the rest take as long as you
      want to give them. It is designed to survive a bad morning.</p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <details>
    <summary>Is this a substitute for therapy?</summary>
    <div class="answer-body">
      <p>No. It is a daily noticing practice, not treatment, and it is not a crisis resource. If
      something it surfaces needs more than a journal, that is useful information and a good
      reason to <a href="/contact/">book a consult</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <details>
    <summary>Do I need to have read it to work with Reem?</summary>
    <div class="answer-body">
      <p>Not at all. Clients and supervisees come to the practice without ever having seen it.
      The book exists for the people who want something to do on their own.</p>
    </div>
  </details>
